<header><p class="st-kicker">crusader state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Toron</h1><p class="st-meta">1105 CE – 1266 CE (approx.) · capital Toron</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Crusader lordship in the hills of southern Lebanon whose lords, the Humphreys of Toron, were among the great barons of Jerusalem.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1105 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-of-saint-omer">Hugh of Saint-Omer</a>, lord of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-galilee">Principality of Galilee</a>, built the castle of Toron at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibnin">Tibnin</a> in the hills above <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tyre">Tyre</a> to support raids on the city, which was still in Muslim hands. It became a lordship held by the Toron family.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humphrey-ii-of-toron">Humphrey II of Toron</a> was constable of the kingdom and a respected negotiator with the Muslims. His grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humphrey-iv-of-toron">Humphrey IV</a> married Isabella, heir to the throne, but refused to be made king in 1186 and later lost her when barons forced their divorce. The lordship controlled hill villages and the routes from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tyre">Tyre</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banias">Banyas</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> took Toron in 1187, and German crusaders failed to retake it in 1197-1198. It was returned by the treaty of 1229 and passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-montfort">Montfort</a> family, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> captured it in 1266. The castle site is still occupied by a later fortress in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibnin">Tibnin</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lordship-of-toron.jpg" alt="Lordship of Toron" width="320" height="258"><figcaption>Image: Charles William Meredith van de Velde · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:37.Kalat-Tibnin_(le_chateau_Toron_des_Croises).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1105 CE – 1266 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>crusader state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Toron</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Humphrey II of Toron, Humphrey IV of Toron, Philip of Montfort</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Latin Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/lebanon">Lebanon</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Toron</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1186&amp;focus=lordship-of-toron" aria-label="Lordship of Toron on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5586 973 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Toron lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5906 1229L5908 1277M5906 1229L5815 1335"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5908 1277h0M5815 1335h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5906 1229h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5906 1229h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1186&amp;focus=lordship-of-toron">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

